Image architecture

Physical image files live only in:

public/images/

Central logical image registry:

src/data/images.js

Flow:

public/images/
      ↓
src/data/images.js
      ↓
services.js / projects.js / sections
      ↓
getImage(...)
      ↓
React component
      ↓
<img>
      ↓
Browser

Important

The physical images were NOT renamed to the logical names.

images.js maps readable logical keys to the actual physical files.

Example:

serviceKitchen: "/images/interior01.jpg"
projectKitchen1: "/images/project01.jpg"
aboutShop: "/images/interior01.jpg"

This lets one physical file be reused in multiple places.

One image = one physical file

Never duplicate the same photograph under multiple filenames.

Bad:

hero01.jpg
about01.jpg
contact01.jpg

when all contain the same photograph.

Good:

hero01.jpg

Reuse the same registry reference wherever needed.

Replacing an image

The simplest client workflow:

Open public/images/.

Find the existing filename.

Replace the image while keeping the same filename.

Example:

public/images/project01.jpg

Replace the photo but keep project01.jpg.

No code change is required because the registry still points to the same path.

Adding a new image

Add one new physical file to public/images/.

Add one logical key to src/data/images.js.

Use the new key from the relevant data file.

Do not create duplicates of existing photographs.

Recommended image sizes

Recommendations only; exact dimensions are not mandatory.

